<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- A message with NO <Document> element at all: the container sits directly
     under the operator's own envelope. issettled and montran RTGS traffic in
     the corpus ships camt.029/056, pacs.002/004/008/009 this way — 17 of the
     214 corpus files. The readers accept these (identity is the container);
     a sniffer that requires <Document> calls them "not ISO 20022" and routes
     nothing.

     The head.001 binding is deliberately declared BEFORE the message binding:
     both are ISO identifiers, and only one of them names the message. -->
